+suggested_file: docs/adr/034-plays-answer-from-memory-inside-a-drive.md
+title: "Inside a Drive, a Play Answers From Memory and Asks Only When Memory Holds Nothing"
+status: Proposed
+date: 2026-10-18
+level: framework
+decided_by: Kapil Ahuja   # the brief's "Decided by"; the Decided by line stays out of the draft while Proposed — adr.py accept --by fills it
+decided_in: "#613 (the Kickoff drive), plan item 1 (.garura/project/issues/613/specs/plan.md), under #594 and business intent #606"
+run: {in_drive: false, issue: 613}   # run.json — run by hand; the person accepts before it is written accepted
+style_reference: docs/adr/032-drive-review-of-outcomes.md   # short sentences, plain words, numbered decision parts (as ADRs 029–033)
+
+# --- Overlaps: adr.py overlaps --adr brief.md --dir docs/adr -> 032 (10.9), 029 (9.03), 033 (5.95),
+# 031 (3.73), 028 (3.48), 026 (3.33). ADR 002 read by hand (named by the caller). Each judged by reading it.
+overlaps:
+  - adr: "029"
+    file: docs/adr/029-drives.md
+    verdict: amended
+    part: >-
+      §2, the bullet "A new question stops it. If a question comes up mid-run that was not
+      answered at the start, the drive stops and asks. It never picks an answer for itself."
+      Now: a play answers a new question from memory and the system, with the source recorded;
+      the question stops the drive and goes to the person only when nothing there supports an
+      answer; never from the model's own knowledge.
+    not_changed: >-
+      §2's other bullets stand: "Questions first" (the answers gathered up front are the first
+      memory a play reads); "No stops for the plays' checkpoints"; "No rules of its own";
+      "Checked by someone else"; the evidence record. The same bullet's last sentence also stands:
+      a drive does not run on a coding agent's own never-stop loop, because that pushes the
+      decision onto the model — this ADR keeps the decision off the model (memory, or the person).
+      §1, §3, §4, §6 not touched.
+  - adr: "032"
+    file: docs/adr/032-drive-review-of-outcomes.md
+    verdict: not affected (relied on)
+    why: >-
+      §2 already says the plays' review records tell the review step "what changed and why";
+      the sources of the answers a play took from memory are part of that "why", and the review
+      shows the person what was assumed. The review stays at the outcome level; no 032 clause
+      changes. The review step and tools are not built yet (#641–#650 in the #613 plan), so they
+      must carry the assumptions when built — named under Work This Creates, not as an amendment.
+  - adr: "033"
+    file: docs/adr/033-approval-in-the-product-model.md
+    verdict: not affected (relied on)
+    why: >-
+      Answers taken from memory land in pieces a play writes; every such piece is changed until
+      a person approves it, so nothing built from an assumption is worked on before a person
+      sees it. No 033 clause changes.
+    open_point: >-
+      The brief counts the product model as memory. ADR 033 §3 lets agents work only on approved
+      pieces. Whether a play may answer a question from a piece that is not yet approved (for
+      example an intent /intent saved as proposed earlier in the same drive) is not settled by
+      the brief. Named as a risk in the draft, not decided.
+  - adr: "031"
+    file: docs/adr/031-business-intent-and-ice.md
+    verdict: not affected (relied on)
+    why: >-
+      §5 says "A drive may ask questions, but /intent inside a drive does not stop for approval" —
+      still true: a drive may still ask (when memory holds nothing), and the approval rule is
+      untouched. §1 "Only a person confirms or drops" a business intent stands: an answer taken
+      from memory never confirms an intent; inside a drive every intent is still saved proposed.
+      The "nothing invented, ask the person" rule for /intent is play intent (/intent C5), not
+      in ADR 031's Decision — it is listed under Affects.
+  - adr: "002"
+    file: docs/adr/002-l1-checkpoint-model.md
+    verdict: not affected
+    why: >-
+      ADR 002 is about checkpoints (artifact + approval), not questions. Rule 2 was already
+      superseded in part by ADR 029 for drives. This ADR changes how a play answers a question,
+      not how a checkpoint is resolved (drive contract rule 3 is not changed by the brief).
+  - adr: "028"
+    file: docs/adr/028-agentic-lifecycle-five-loops.md
+    verdict: not affected
+    why: "The five loops and their recipes; nothing on how a play answers questions. Shares only the /intent name."
+  - adr: "026"
+    file: docs/adr/026-direct-to-model-writes.md
+    verdict: not affected
+    why: "Write-then-review stands; this ADR does not change where or how a play writes the model."
+supersedes: []
+amends:
+  - {adr: "029", part: "§2 \"A new question stops it\": inside a drive a play answers from memory and the system, recording each answer's source, and the question stops the drive only when nothing there supports an answer; never from the model's own knowledge"}
