+# --- ICE impact (from each play's ICE source; ontology.md ICE kind read — unchanged)
+ice_impact: >-
+  The agent intents of the plays that run inside a drive change. /intent (C4, C5, Step 3): inside
+  a drive it answers its open questions from memory and the system first, records each answer's
+  source, and asks the person only what nothing supports; C5's "every property traces to the
+  source or the person's answers" widens, inside a drive, to the memory this ADR names, each with
+  its source. /vision (C11) and /understand (C13): "a question neither the contract nor the model
+  answers stops the run" widens to all of memory and the system. /adr (C5): its business-intent
+  stop stays, on ADR 031's rule rather than ADR 029 §2. The Kickoff drive (#613) stops mid-run
+  only for a question nothing in memory supports. Run by hand, no play changes. The ICE kind
+  does not change (ontology.md: its properties and rules say nothing on how a question is
+  answered).
+
+# --- Business-intent check
+business_intent_check: none
+business_intent_check_reason: >-
+  A framework rule about how plays answer questions inside a drive. No person's business intent
+  changes; nothing under product-os/intents/ is named or written. The Business Intent kind's rules
+  in ontology.md do not change either: they say nothing about where a draft's properties come
+  from, and "Only a person confirms or drops it; an agent never does" stands — inside a drive
+  every intent is still saved proposed and confirmed or dropped by a person at the drive's review
+  (ADR 031 §5, ADR 032 §4). Edge for the person to see: inside a drive /intent may now fill a
+  proposed intent's why, who asked or proof from memory (with its source) instead of asking; if
+  the person reads ADR 031 §1 ("an outcome in their words") as kind doctrine this touches, the
+  check would be `kind`, not `instance`.
+
+# --- Open points the brief does not settle (named, not decided — do not invent an answer)
+open_points:
+  - >-
+    Pinned checkpoints. The brief changes drive contract rule 4 only. Rule 3 says a pinned
